I left out the `aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0` import. The node's `with` clause is its entire authority, and it grants only `kb-read` and `tool-llm`. The graph definition hasn't been updated yet, and the enrichment call would send the user's question text to an external host that this node isn't authorized to reach. Once the graph is updated to grant `http-client`, that import and call can be added. The blocks below implement the node as currently granted. The note above the blocks is outside the two files, so it's only for you.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{conversation-context, response-result};

    import aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0;
    import aap:caps/tool-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(ctx: conversation-context) -> response-result;
}
